    "raw": "Phase change: 1235.08 K, melting point of Ag; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.700$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 8.865 + 0.196 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.457 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=8.865\\times10^{-3}T+0.098\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.457\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.805$ \nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1235.08 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hf}^{\\circ} = 74.950 - 0.022 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.072 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 45.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 74.950 + 0.022 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 1.072 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 22.650 T^{-1} - 24.544 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \n1235.08-2000 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 74.237 - 2.750 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.153 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 23.100 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 74.237 + 2.750 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 0.153 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 11.550 T^{-1} - 42.246 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
